---
title: User needs
description: The user needs that the Intent capture work is attempting to satisfy.
permalink: /userneeds/
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% from "nhsuk/components/tables/macro.njk" import table as nhsukTable %}

{% block content %}

  {{ appDocumentHeader({
    title: title,
    description: description
  }) }}

  <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
      <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
          <p>User needs describe what people need from the service in order to make progress safely and confidently. They are not the same as intents. A user need describes the outcome a person needs; an intent describes what they are trying to do or express at a particular point in the journey.</p>

          <p>For this work, user needs help keep the design grounded in people’s goals rather than NHS service structures. They should be reviewed as the team learns more from research, pilots and operational evidence.</p>
      </div>
  </div>

  {% set tableRows = [] %}
  {% for need in collections.userNeeds | sort(false, true, 'page.fileSlug') %}
    {% set clausesHtml %}
      {% if need.data.acceptanceClauses | length %}
        <ul class="nhsuk-list nhsuk-list--bullet nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-0">
          {% for clause in need.data.acceptanceClauses %}
            <li>{{ clause }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      {% endif %}
    {% endset %}
    {% set tableRows = tableRows.concat([[
      { text: need.data.userType },
      { text: need.data.need },
      { text: need.data.reason },
      { html: clausesHtml }
    ]]) %}
  {% endfor %}

  {{ nhsukTable({
    responsive: true,
    head: [
      { text: "As a" },
      { text: "I need" },
      { text: "So that" },
      { text: "Satisfied when" }
    ],
    rows: tableRows
  }) }}
{% endblock %}
